{# Format and surface the finalized Sankey as the process's final output.
[inference]
   This is a pure Jinja2 template (no frontmatter) executed by the `render` action.
   It wraps the adapt step's mermaid source in a titled, annotated document with:
   - A title derived from domain + subject
   - A description paragraph (domain, weight unit, conservation mode, ontology)
   - The Mermaid sankey-beta diagram in a fenced code block
   - A flow annotation table (source → target, weight, provenance)
   - A conservation check line
   - A notes section (abbreviations, placeholders, structural deviations)
   - An output path for file save

   Deterministic — no LLM call. All formatting is Jinja2 template logic. #}

{# ── Title ── #}
{%- set domain_title = domain | replace("-", " ") | title -%}
{%- set subject_title = subject | replace("-", " ") | title -%}

# {{ domain_title }}: {{ subject_title }}

{# ── Description ── #}

This diagram visualizes a {{ domain | replace("-", " ") }} flow with {{ node_count }} nodes and {{ edge_count }} edges. Weights are in {{ weight_unit }}. Conservation mode: **{{ conservation_mode }}**{% if conservation_mode == "mandatory" %} — inflow equals outflow at every internal node.{% elif conservation_mode == "asserted" %} — conservation may or may not hold; discrepancies are flagged.{% elif conservation_mode == "none" %} — flows are not conserved; asymmetry is intentional and not balanced with fabricated loss branches.{% endif %}

{# ── Mermaid diagram ── #}

```mermaid
{{ mermaid_source }}
```

{# ── Flow annotations ── #}

| Source | Target | Weight | Notes |
|--------|--------|--------|-------|
{%- for edge in edges %}
| {{ edge.source }} | {{ edge.target }} | {{ edge.weight }} | {{ edge.weight_source | default("(not specified)") }} |
{%- endfor %}

{# ── Conservation check ── #}

**Conservation:** {{ conservation_check }}

{# ── Notes ── #}
{% if adapt_notes %}

**Notes:** {{ adapt_notes }}
{% endif %}

---

Output path: {{ output_path | default("(not specified)") }}